}

docs {
  # Update Blog Post
  
  Updates an existing blog post's title, description, and/or attached document. All fields are optional — only provided fields are updated.
  
  ## Endpoint
  `PATCH /api/v1/blogs/:id`
  
  ## Authorization
  Inherited — requires authentication.
  
  ## Path Parameters
  
  | Param | Type   | Required | Constraints | Description                    |
  | :---- | :----- | :------- | :---------- | :----------------------------- |
  | id    | string | Yes      | Valid UUID   | The unique ID of the blog post. |
  
  ## Request Body (`multipart/form-data`)
  
  | Field       | Type   | Required | Constraints | Description                                  |
  | :---------- | :----- | :------- | :---------- | :------------------------------------------- |
  | title       | string | No       | —           | Updated title for the blog post.             |
  | description | string | No       | —           | Updated description for the blog post.       |
  | file        | file   | No       | Max: 20 MB  | Replacement document file. Old file is deleted from Cloudinary. |
  
  ## Success Response
  - **Status Code**: `200 OK`
  - **Body**:
    ```json
    {
      "success": true,
      "message": "Blog post updated successfully",
      "data": null
    }
    ```
  
  ## Error Responses
  - **400 Bad Request**: Validation failed (e.g., `id` is not a valid UUID).
  - **500 Internal Server Error**: Blog not found, or Cloudinary upload/delete failed.
  
  ## Notes
  - If a new `file` is provided, the existing document is first deleted from Cloudinary before the new one is uploaded.
  - If only `title` and/or `description` are provided (no file), only the text fields are updated.
  - If neither `title` nor `description` is provided and no file is attached, the endpoint returns `200 OK` with no changes.
  - The cache entry `cedarrise:blogs:single:{id}` is invalidated after a successful update.
}
